WEBVTT

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.969
Senate committee. Education

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.771
Committee will come to order.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.773
Good morning everybody, welcome

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.374
to this informational hearing

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.808
here in this very impressive

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.910
venue, I will say locker rooms

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.679
have come a long way since my

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:13.313
playing days as starting forward

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.048
on the Millbrook High School

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.750
soccer team, and if we're really

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.918
doing this right, we'd have

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:19.519
somebody singing the national

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:20.920
anthem, but let's begin the

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.989
hearing. So first, let me begin

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.891
my comments by thanking the Los

00:00:24.958 --> 00:00:26.659
Angeles 84 Foundation for all of

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:28.661
its support and assistance in

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:29.195
developing this morning's

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:30.897
informational hearing, ensuring

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.766
that students and all children

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:34.734
have adequate play and access to

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.770
physical activity is essential

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:37.270
to a child's social and

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.671
emotional development. And

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.673
health, second, I'd like to

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.241
thank Kevin Demoff and the

00:00:41.307 --> 00:00:44.711
entire Los Angeles Rams

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:45.278
organization for generously

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.780
hosting this important

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.715
conversation here at SoFi

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.850
Stadium today, and I'm very

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:54.687
proud to serve as the chair of

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:55.255
the Senate California State

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.823
Senate Committee on Education.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.758
Last year, among the bills I

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.627
authored was a measure, SB 291,

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.629
which addressed inconsistencies

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.296
and inequities in schools across

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:06.800
the state with regard to recess

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:07.434
to ensure that every California

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.035
student can be assured of access

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:11.004
to at least 30 minutes of recess

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:12.772
in a standard school day so as

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:14.808
to benefit from the benefits

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:15.408
that accrue from unstructured

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.943
play and decompression, that

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.713
only recess provides and which

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:21.314
an extensive body of research

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.916
has validated. Today's hearing

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.818
on physical fitness and play is

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.786
a natural next step in that

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:27.320
broader conversation as we

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.855
endeavor to build on that

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.723
success and explore ways to

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.357
bring young people opportunities

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.625
for play that will offer

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.661
pathways to personal growth.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:35.128
While addressing the

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:35.695
disconcerting trend toward

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.963
inactivity, obesity, and other

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.998
behavioral issues among young

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:40.900
people that robust physical

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:41.434
activity has been found to

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.604
offset. The title of today's

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.104
informational hearing is

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.773
Examining Physical Education

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:47.407
through a Play Equity Framework.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:50.610
Today's hearing will also serve

00:01:50.677 --> 00:01:52.745
as the official release of the

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:53.313
2024 California Play Equity

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.914
Report. The first of its kind

00:01:54.981 --> 00:01:56.616
commissioned by the La84

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.618
Foundation, the report provides

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:00.854
a statewide look at play, equity

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:01.454
and insights into the barriers

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:04.624
of sport, play and movement for

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:05.258
kids. The report also examines

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.126
the landscape of youth sports

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.728
participation and physical

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.730
activity across the state, with

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.732
a specific focus on underserved

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:13.299
communities and the barriers

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:14.801
that they face. The report's

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:15.401
findings are both eye opening

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.170
and inspiring, revealing both

00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:18.838
some of the pressing challenges

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:19.339
currently preventing all

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:20.740
children from fully benefiting

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.609
from play, sports and physical

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:23.243
activity, while also showcasing

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.044
the promise of youth

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:25.578
participation in physical

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:29.082
activity. As part of today's

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:30.650
hearing agenda, the committee

00:02:30.717 --> 00:02:31.251
will have the opportunity to

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.919
hear highlights of the report

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:33.486
and a presentation from the

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:34.954
Legislative Analyst's Office on

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.856
Physical Education, PE funding

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:37.423
in California. In the last

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.092
section of the hearing, we will

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.894
also hear from a panel of

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:41.427
experts on the benefits of

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.129
physical activity and physical

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:43.696
education for students and

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.031
communities. In a moment, I'm

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:48.735
going to turn the floor over to

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.302
Mr. Kevin Demoff of the Los

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:52.805
Angeles Rams and then to a man

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:53.273
who probably needs no

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:54.941
