00:21:10.068 --> 00:21:12.137
we've gained the benefit of

00:21:12.204 --> 00:21:15.874
decades and decades and

00:21:15.941 --> 00:21:16.475
generations and generations of

00:21:16.541 --> 00:21:18.110
resources and programs and teams

00:21:18.176 --> 00:21:22.280
and systems being created for us

00:21:22.347 --> 00:21:25.951
to get to where we want to go.

00:21:26.018 --> 00:21:28.120
For 53 men that that control

00:21:28.186 --> 00:21:29.888
this locker room week in and

00:21:29.955 --> 00:21:31.990
week out, that access in a lot

00:21:32.057 --> 00:21:34.259
of ways, has always been there

00:21:34.326 --> 00:21:35.961
for them. We've always invested

00:21:36.028 --> 00:21:36.561
in peewee football on the boys

00:21:36.628 --> 00:21:39.798
side. We've always invested in

00:21:39.865 --> 00:21:40.432
boys and girls club basketball

00:21:40.499 --> 00:21:42.401
on the boys side, we've always

00:21:42.467 --> 00:21:43.869
invested in high level

00:21:43.935 --> 00:21:44.469
basketball, football, soccer,

00:21:44.536 --> 00:21:48.040
baseball on the boys side. But

00:21:48.106 --> 00:21:48.573
we're also lagging in our

00:21:48.640 --> 00:21:52.144
commitment to young girls and

00:21:52.210 --> 00:21:53.979
young women when it comes to

00:21:54.046 --> 00:21:54.613
access to sport. And that also

00:21:54.680 --> 00:21:58.250
then plays a role in why it is

00:21:58.316 --> 00:22:00.252
inequitable currently and why we

00:22:00.318 --> 00:22:02.120
have to continue to invest in a

00:22:02.187 --> 00:22:04.356
major way. Because yes, it lifts

00:22:04.423 --> 00:22:06.158
our boys up. But we also know as

00:22:06.224 --> 00:22:08.260
we sit here in the state of

00:22:08.326 --> 00:22:11.997
California with a woman of color

00:22:12.064 --> 00:22:15.901
potentially running for and

00:22:15.967 --> 00:22:18.103
being a part of the largest

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:20.038
conversation we can have around

00:22:20.105 --> 00:22:20.572
what it means to have an

00:22:20.639 --> 00:22:22.174
opportunity, regardless of

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:26.144
gender. Sport is the way that we

00:22:26.211 --> 00:22:27.879
can have that conversation here

00:22:27.946 --> 00:22:30.182
in the state of California for

00:22:30.248 --> 00:22:31.950
our young girls now, so that our

00:22:32.017 --> 00:22:32.517
young girls now can grow up

00:22:32.584 --> 00:22:34.319
seeing and believing that she

00:22:34.386 --> 00:22:36.388
can access the best parts of who

00:22:36.455 --> 00:22:38.356
she is, and that we don't see

00:22:38.423 --> 00:22:40.225
that drop off that starts to

00:22:40.292 --> 00:22:42.227
happen at 11, 12 years old for

00:22:42.294 --> 00:22:44.329
many of our young girls, because

00:22:44.396 --> 00:22:46.064
as the report, you know,

00:22:46.131 --> 00:22:47.966
expresses, whether it's lack of

00:22:48.033 --> 00:22:49.935
fun, lack of engagement, which

00:22:50.001 --> 00:22:52.170
obviously as a coach speaks to

00:22:52.237 --> 00:22:55.974
part of the investment in

00:22:56.041 --> 00:22:56.608
resources goes to being able to

00:22:56.675 --> 00:22:58.343
bring in quality people that

00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:00.078
coach and teach our young

00:23:00.145 --> 00:23:02.314
people. And we're not leaning on

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:04.282
our parents who are already

00:23:04.349 --> 00:23:07.886
paying too much for access to

00:23:07.953 --> 00:23:08.520
sports also. Then we're asking

00:23:08.587 --> 00:23:10.222
