00:32:16.768 --> 00:32:18.503
research methodology. We spoke

00:32:18.569 --> 00:32:20.772
with over 1600 parents

00:32:20.838 --> 00:32:22.774
throughout the state of school

00:32:22.840 --> 00:32:23.408
aged children, which represented

00:32:23.474 --> 00:32:28.780
a total of over 2600 youth in

00:32:28.846 --> 00:32:32.450
all regions. We conducted the

00:32:32.517 --> 00:32:33.084
research in just at the end of

00:32:33.151 --> 00:32:36.621
spring in May. The margin of

00:32:36.688 --> 00:32:38.823
error associated with the parent

00:32:38.890 --> 00:32:40.525
data is around 2.4%, plus or

00:32:40.591 --> 00:32:42.894
minus a percentage points. It

00:32:42.960 --> 00:32:46.564
was an online survey then that

00:32:46.631 --> 00:32:47.198
included reaching out to parents

00:32:47.265 --> 00:32:48.733
on mobile devices and text to

00:32:48.800 --> 00:32:52.637
web, and the results here have

00:32:52.704 --> 00:32:53.171
been weighted to match the

00:32:53.237 --> 00:32:54.772
distribution of youth and

00:32:54.839 --> 00:32:58.576
parents across the state.

00:32:58.643 --> 00:33:00.545
Getting into the key findings,

00:33:00.611 --> 00:33:01.079
one of the most striking

00:33:01.145 --> 00:33:02.814
elements of this research is the

00:33:02.880 --> 00:33:06.718
fact that California youth are

00:33:06.784 --> 00:33:08.553
not playing enough. The daily

00:33:08.619 --> 00:33:10.555
activities for California youth

00:33:10.621 --> 00:33:12.824
fall below the recommended CDC

00:33:12.890 --> 00:33:14.759
