01:29:48.049 --> 01:29:48.649
the final member of our panel is

01:29:48.716 --> 01:29:50.351
Doctor William Parham, who is a

01:29:50.418 --> 01:29:52.286
professor of in the counseling

01:29:52.353 --> 01:29:53.921
program and director of the

01:29:53.988 --> 01:29:54.555
School of Education center for

01:29:54.622 --> 01:29:56.057
Trauma Informed Education at

01:29:56.124 --> 01:29:56.624
Loyola marymount University.

01:29:56.691 --> 01:29:59.994
Doctor Parham also serves as the

01:30:00.061 --> 01:30:02.063
inaugural director of the Mental

01:30:02.130 --> 01:30:02.697
Health and Wellness Program for

01:30:02.764 --> 01:30:03.331
the National Basketball Players

01:30:03.397 --> 01:30:04.232
Association. Among his many past

01:30:04.298 --> 01:30:07.935
achievements is his service as a

01:30:08.002 --> 01:30:08.436
member of the California

01:30:08.503 --> 01:30:09.937
Governor's Council on Physical

01:30:10.004 --> 01:30:10.571
Fitness and Mental Well-Being,

01:30:10.638 --> 01:30:12.273
as well as a as a member of the

01:30:12.340 --> 01:30:13.941
California Science Foundation.

01:30:14.008 --> 01:30:16.110
Science of sport Advisory

01:30:16.177 --> 01:30:16.711
Committee. Welcome, everyone,

01:30:16.778 --> 01:30:19.947
and, Miss Schimmel, if you

01:30:20.014 --> 01:30:20.548
wouldn't mind kicking us off,

01:30:20.615 --> 01:30:22.483
please begin when you're ready.

01:30:22.550 --> 01:30:24.352
Well, thank you, thank you,

01:30:24.418 --> 01:30:25.953
Senator Newman, for that

01:30:26.020 --> 01:30:26.587
introduction. And permit me by

01:30:26.654 --> 01:30:28.156
first starting, starting out by

01:30:28.222 --> 01:30:30.158
thanking the Los Angeles Rams

01:30:30.224 --> 01:30:30.792
for hosting this, convening my

01:30:30.858 --> 01:30:34.395
team at the LA 84 Foundation,

01:30:34.462 --> 01:30:36.030
and specifically Fernando

01:30:36.097 --> 01:30:36.597
Ramirez, who led efforts in

01:30:36.664 --> 01:30:38.199
partnership with your office to

01:30:38.266 --> 01:30:42.270
put this hearing on. And to my

01:30:42.336 --> 01:30:46.040
friends and colleagues, Senator

01:30:46.107 --> 01:30:46.507
Bradford, Senator Lola

01:30:46.574 --> 01:30:48.042
Smallwood, my friends and my

01:30:48.109 --> 01:30:48.643
colleagues on this committee,

01:30:48.709 --> 01:30:50.211
thank you for your bold

01:30:50.278 --> 01:30:52.113
leadership today. Today's

01:30:52.180 --> 01:30:52.580
education hearing is a

01:30:52.647 --> 01:30:54.182
significant milestone in the pay

01:30:54.248 --> 01:30:56.250
equity movement. When we started

01:30:56.317 --> 01:30:58.186
this movement six years ago, we

01:30:58.252 --> 01:31:00.087
said that pay equity was a

01:31:00.154 --> 01:31:00.688
crisis hiding in plain sight.

01:31:00.755 --> 01:31:04.058
I'm honored today to say that it

01:31:04.125 --> 01:31:04.659
is no longer hiding in plain

01:31:04.725 --> 01:31:06.394
sight. We're bringing it out to

01:31:06.460 --> 01:31:08.196
the forefront and the actions

01:31:08.262 --> 01:31:08.796
that we will continue to take

01:31:08.863 --> 01:31:10.431
together, I believe, will change

01:31:10.498 --> 01:31:12.266
the trajectory of California

01:31:12.333 --> 01:31:14.268
youth far into the future, and,

01:31:14.335 --> 01:31:16.404
you know, on a personal note, I

01:31:16.470 --> 01:31:18.406
was one of those statistics you

01:31:18.472 --> 01:31:20.208
heard me speak of earlier today.

01:31:20.274 --> 01:31:20.842
A girl from Carson, California,

01:31:20.908 --> 01:31:24.078
just down the 110 freeway or the

01:31:24.145 --> 01:31:26.047
405 freeway, depending on which

01:31:26.113 --> 01:31:26.581
way you go, navigating the

01:31:26.647 --> 01:31:28.249
perils of economic barriers,

01:31:28.316 --> 01:31:32.086
mental health challenges, gangs

01:31:32.153 --> 01:31:34.255
and drugs within my own family

01:31:34.322 --> 01:31:36.390
and within my community. But I

01:31:36.457 --> 01:31:38.059
was fortunate to benefit from

01:31:38.125 --> 01:31:40.161
the power of sport, play and

01:31:40.228 --> 01:31:40.761
movement in my public school,

01:31:40.828 --> 01:31:44.198
Lakewood Elementary. Carson

01:31:44.265 --> 01:31:44.799
Curtis Junior High School, and

01:31:44.866 --> 01:31:46.400
ultimately Carson High School,

01:31:46.467 --> 01:31:48.469
where I played baseball. And

01:31:48.536 --> 01:31:50.238
excuse me, I didn't play

01:31:50.304 --> 01:31:52.306
baseball, but I did play

01:31:52.373 --> 01:31:52.907
baseball, but basketball and

01:31:52.974 --> 01:31:54.242
tennis. And it was through PE

01:31:54.308 --> 01:31:56.077
and middle school that I was

01:31:56.143 --> 01:31:56.644
able to sample a variety of

01:31:56.711 --> 01:32:00.214
sports to find what I was good

01:32:00.281 --> 01:32:00.815
at. But sport also helped me

01:32:00.882 --> 01:32:02.550
find my strength and my voice to

01:32:02.617 --> 01:32:04.385
navigate these obstacles in my

01:32:04.452 --> 01:32:06.454
family and my communities and

01:32:06.520 --> 01:32:08.222
build pathways to an

01:32:08.289 --> 01:32:10.091
extraordinarily enriched life.

01:32:10.157 --> 01:32:10.625
Sports kept me engaged in

01:32:10.691 --> 01:32:14.061
school. In fact, it was the only

01:32:14.128 --> 01:32:14.629
reason that I showed up for

01:32:14.695 --> 01:32:16.497
school on some days, and as it

01:32:16.564 --> 01:32:18.466
turns out, sport sports were

01:32:18.532 --> 01:32:20.067
absolutely seminal for me,

01:32:20.134 --> 01:32:22.370
developing resiliency that I

01:32:22.436 --> 01:32:24.538
needed to make it through Army's

01:32:24.605 --> 01:32:26.374
basic training, which ultimately

01:32:26.440 --> 01:32:28.242
became my pathway to college.

01:32:28.309 --> 01:32:28.709
And I can say without

01:32:28.776 --> 01:32:32.213
equivocation that I would not be

01:32:32.280 --> 01:32:32.847
here in front of this committee

01:32:32.914 --> 01:32:34.582
if it weren't for sport and

01:32:34.649 --> 01:32:36.384
movement in my life. So I'm

01:32:36.450 --> 01:32:38.419
humbled to serve as the

01:32:38.486 --> 01:32:40.288
president and CEO of the L84

01:32:40.354 --> 01:32:42.256
Foundation, a legacy of the 1984

01:32:42.323 --> 01:32:42.890
Olympic Games. It's celebrating

01:32:42.957 --> 01:32:44.492
40 years this year, and with the

01:32:44.558 --> 01:32:48.262
FIFA World Cup 26 and the LA 28

01:32:48.329 --> 01:32:50.331
Olympics and Paralympic Games on

01:32:50.398 --> 01:32:52.233
the horizon, we are a model for

01:32:52.300 --> 01:32:54.468
what long term impact looks like

01:32:54.535 --> 01:32:56.437
resulting from major sporting

01:32:56.504 --> 01:32:58.306
events in our state. And for

01:32:58.372 --> 01:32:58.906
four decades, we have helped

01:32:58.973 --> 01:33:02.176
build pathways to enrich lives

01:33:02.243 --> 01:33:02.677
through sport, play and

01:33:02.743 --> 01:33:04.345
movement. For millions of school

01:33:04.412 --> 01:33:04.946
aged children. We have trained

01:33:05.012 --> 01:33:06.380
thousands of coaches and rebuilt

01:33:06.447 --> 01:33:08.449
safe, public safe spaces for

01:33:08.516 --> 01:33:10.584
kids to play throughout the

01:33:10.651 --> 01:33:14.455
region, and we commissioned this

01:33:14.522 --> 01:33:16.190
2024 California Play Equity

01:33:16.257 --> 01:33:18.392
Report with one specific

01:33:18.459 --> 01:33:22.363
objective in mind to deepen the

01:33:22.430 --> 01:33:24.298
impact of our work and to close

01:33:24.365 --> 01:33:26.367
the play equity gap. And I

01:33:26.434 --> 01:33:28.636
invite the committee to reflect

01:33:28.703 --> 01:33:30.271
on three takeaways today one,

01:33:30.338 --> 01:33:32.473
the power of joy and fun two

01:33:32.540 --> 01:33:36.310
advancing a play equity

01:33:36.377 --> 01:33:36.911
framework in our policymaking

01:33:36.978 --> 01:33:40.314
and three political will, joy

01:33:40.381 --> 01:33:44.352
and fun. As you've heard earlier

01:33:44.418 --> 01:33:44.919
today, the time commitment

01:33:44.986 --> 01:33:46.487
required to continue playing

01:33:46.554 --> 01:33:48.556
loss of interest friends,

01:33:48.622 --> 01:33:49.123
quitting and competitiveness

01:33:49.190 --> 01:33:52.393
emerge as the top reasons that

01:33:52.460 --> 01:33:54.161
it had a significant impact on

01:33:54.228 --> 01:33:56.263
youth leaving sports. We can't

01:33:56.330 --> 01:33:58.366
ignore the significant

01:33:58.432 --> 01:33:58.933
differences in dropout rates

01:33:59.000 --> 01:34:00.434
reported across race and

01:34:00.501 --> 01:34:04.405
ethnicity and gender, but I was

01:34:04.472 --> 01:34:06.273
particularly struck by the fact

01:34:06.340 --> 01:34:08.609
that 2 in 5 parents, nearly 43%,

01:34:08.676 --> 01:34:10.311
say that sports was no longer

01:34:10.378 --> 01:34:12.279
fun for their children. As a

01:34:12.346 --> 01:34:14.548
nation, we need fun and joy in

01:34:14.615 --> 01:34:16.450
our lives and our and in our

01:34:16.517 --> 01:34:18.285
communities. Now more than ever,

01:34:18.352 --> 01:34:20.521
our U.S. Surgeon General has

01:34:20.588 --> 01:34:22.323
raised that as a nation, we are

01:34:22.390 --> 01:34:22.957
socially disconnected and facing

01:34:23.024 --> 01:34:24.592
an isolation epidemic, and our

01:34:24.658 --> 01:34:28.429
youth are at the epicenter of

01:34:28.496 --> 01:34:30.398
this isolation in a

01:34:30.464 --> 01:34:31.032
disproportionate amount of kids

01:34:31.098 --> 01:34:32.500
of color are struggling with

01:34:32.566 --> 01:34:36.470
stress, anxiety, and depression.

01:34:36.537 --> 01:34:38.606
My own son being one of them.

01:34:38.672 --> 01:34:40.341
Sports bridges divides and

01:34:40.408 --> 01:34:42.309
brings people together and in

01:34:42.376 --> 01:34:44.578
the right environment with

01:34:44.645 --> 01:34:45.179
caring adults. Play in sports

01:34:45.246 --> 01:34:48.349
can serve as an arena of

01:34:48.416 --> 01:34:50.284
belonging. It creates a level of

01:34:50.351 --> 01:34:52.286
spontaneous co-creation and

01:34:52.353 --> 01:34:54.388
interaction. We saw that today

01:34:54.455 --> 01:34:54.855
with Playworks and the

01:34:54.922 --> 01:34:56.457
demonstration we did in just ten

01:34:56.524 --> 01:34:58.459
simple minutes and it builds

01:34:58.526 --> 01:35:00.561
community in the process. We

01:35:00.628 --> 01:35:02.663
need to provide more time for

01:35:02.730 --> 01:35:04.365
children to experience the joy

01:35:04.432 --> 01:35:06.467
of community through sport and

01:35:06.534 --> 01:35:10.304
play. And how do we do that? I

01:35:10.371 --> 01:35:10.938
believe we do that through play

01:35:11.005 --> 01:35:12.706
equity. As a framework. We need

01:35:12.773 --> 01:35:14.475
to lead from a play equity

01:35:14.542 --> 01:35:16.510
centered framework in all of our

01:35:16.577 --> 01:35:18.646
policy work in the state of

01:35:18.712 --> 01:35:20.481
California, and play equity as

01:35:20.548 --> 01:35:22.349
it was mentioned earlier, is the

01:35:22.416 --> 01:35:22.950
concept of ensuring that all

01:35:23.017 --> 01:35:24.685
children, regardless of their

01:35:24.752 --> 01:35:26.287
backgrounds, have equality of

01:35:26.353 --> 01:35:28.322
access to play opportunities,

01:35:28.389 --> 01:35:28.889
sports programs and healthy

01:35:28.956 --> 01:35:30.391
movement. It recognizes that

01:35:30.458 --> 01:35:32.726
sport and play are essential for

01:35:32.793 --> 01:35:34.495
a child's physical, emotional,

01:35:34.562 --> 01:35:38.532
social and academic development,

01:35:38.599 --> 01:35:39.100
and that disparities across

01:35:39.166 --> 01:35:42.303
sports and play have perpetuated

01:35:42.369 --> 01:35:44.572
inequalities in other areas of

01:35:44.638 --> 01:35:46.474
life as well. Rates of physical

01:35:46.540 --> 01:35:48.509
activity are lowest for black

01:35:48.576 --> 01:35:50.511
and brown girls, youth with

01:35:50.578 --> 01:35:51.045
disability and low income

01:35:51.112 --> 01:35:52.580
households. As you heard

01:35:52.646 --> 01:35:56.350
Sha'carri mentioned today, this

01:35:56.417 --> 01:35:56.984
means that we must center those

01:35:57.051 --> 01:35:58.652
on the margin in our policy

01:35:58.719 --> 01:35:59.320
making and to rethink the school

01:35:59.386 --> 01:36:02.289
day to prioritize and to make

01:36:02.356 --> 01:36:04.558
time for sport, play and

01:36:04.625 --> 01:36:06.560
movement and the final point is

01:36:06.627 --> 01:36:10.297
political will. I would put

01:36:10.364 --> 01:36:10.898
forth that political will is

01:36:10.965 --> 01:36:12.533
key. The policies and

01:36:12.600 --> 01:36:13.100
legislations that we put in

01:36:13.167 --> 01:36:14.468
place that are

01:36:14.535 --> 01:36:15.102
disproportionately creating this

01:36:15.169 --> 01:36:18.606
play equity gap are the same

01:36:18.672 --> 01:36:20.374
political will that we can

01:36:20.441 --> 01:36:22.510
address to fix them. So today's

01:36:22.576 --> 01:36:24.645
hearing is a great step toward

01:36:24.712 --> 01:36:26.580
moving this work in action,

01:36:26.647 --> 01:36:28.382
greater funding for sport and

01:36:28.449 --> 01:36:30.417
play in initiatives that focus

01:36:30.484 --> 01:36:31.051
on equity will not only improve

01:36:31.118 --> 01:36:32.686
access to sports and physical

01:36:32.753 --> 01:36:34.522
activity for our youth

01:36:34.588 --> 01:36:34.989
experience inequitable

01:36:35.055 --> 01:36:38.492
opportunities, but it will

01:36:38.559 --> 01:36:40.594
further ease the barriers of a

01:36:40.661 --> 01:36:41.162
parent's economic burden by

01:36:41.228 --> 01:36:44.298
providing more resources for

01:36:44.365 --> 01:36:44.899
childcare in an after school

01:36:44.965 --> 01:36:46.800
setting. Parents overwhelmingly

01:36:46.867 --> 01:36:50.638
support action by the state of

01:36:50.704 --> 01:36:51.172
California to provide full

01:36:51.238 --> 01:36:52.740
funding to support to full

01:36:52.806 --> 01:36:54.675
funding to support structured

01:36:54.742 --> 01:36:56.477
play and physical activity. As

01:36:56.544 --> 01:37:00.548
you heard earlier, nearly 95% of

01:37:00.614 --> 01:37:02.683
parents believe it is important

01:37:02.750 --> 01:37:04.485
for the state of California to

01:37:04.552 --> 01:37:05.085
provide full funding for youth

01:37:05.152 --> 01:37:06.787
sports. PE and structured play.

01:37:06.854 --> 01:37:10.658
Likewise, an overwhelming

01:37:10.724 --> 01:37:12.593
majority of parents, 86% said,

01:37:12.660 --> 01:37:13.127
as you heard, support more

01:37:13.194 --> 01:37:16.530
funding at the state level and

01:37:16.597 --> 01:37:18.399
local level for play equity

01:37:18.465 --> 01:37:18.899
initiatives that expand

01:37:18.966 --> 01:37:20.434
opportunities for all young

01:37:20.501 --> 01:37:22.403
people. Leadership matters, and

01:37:22.469 --> 01:37:24.905
I'm inspired by the leadership

01:37:24.972 --> 01:37:26.540
that this committee is taking

01:37:26.607 --> 01:37:28.709
today. And let me close you with

01:37:28.776 --> 01:37:30.844
this. Thank you. Thank you for

01:37:30.911 --> 01:37:32.580
prioritizing this crucial

01:37:32.646 --> 01:37:34.548
conversation. Thank you for all

01:37:34.615 --> 01:37:35.182
of you who are in the audience.

01:37:35.249 --> 01:37:36.550
Many organizations that we've

01:37:36.617 --> 01:37:38.819
worked with over the last ten

01:37:38.886 --> 01:37:40.688
years since I've been leading

01:37:40.754 --> 01:37:42.423
this organization, to close the

01:37:42.489 --> 01:37:44.425
play equity gap. I think

01:37:44.491 --> 01:37:44.992
together we can ensure that

01:37:45.059 --> 01:37:46.594
every child, regardless of their

01:37:46.660 --> 01:37:48.529
zip code, can move, play and

01:37:48.596 --> 01:37:50.864
thrive. Together, we can build a

01:37:50.931 --> 01:37:52.433
future where equitable access to

01:37:52.499 --> 01:37:52.967
physical education isn't a

01:37:53.033 --> 01:37:56.570
privilege, but it's a right that

01:37:56.637 --> 01:37:58.606
every child has because the

01:37:58.672 --> 01:38:00.474
health and the potential of our

01:38:00.541 --> 01:38:02.409
children depend on it. So thank

01:38:02.476 --> 01:38:06.680
you. Thank you. And thank you.

01:38:06.747 --> 01:38:08.816
And Mr. Paulo, welcome. Please

01:38:08.882 --> 01:38:12.519
proceed. Thank you so much,

01:38:12.586 --> 01:38:13.187
hello. My name is Arden Paula. I

01:38:13.254 --> 01:38:16.423
am 15 years old, going on 16, I

01:38:16.490 --> 01:38:18.659
live at Francis Park. I go to

01:38:18.726 --> 01:38:20.628
San Diego, I go to Francis

01:38:20.694 --> 01:38:22.563
Parker High School, the reason

01:38:22.630 --> 01:38:24.498
I'm here today is to talk a bit

01:38:24.565 --> 01:38:25.099
about my organization that I

01:38:25.165 --> 01:38:26.734
started three years ago, sports

01:38:26.800 --> 01:38:28.769
for kids, and our mission is to

01:38:28.836 --> 01:38:30.904
allow youth volunteers to better

01:38:30.971 --> 01:38:32.673
the lives of the low income and

01:38:32.740 --> 01:38:33.274
homeless through athletics and

01:38:33.340 --> 01:38:36.677
community engagement. My story

01:38:36.744 --> 01:38:38.812
started when I first volunteered

01:38:38.879 --> 01:38:40.414
at a title one elementary school

01:38:40.481 --> 01:38:41.081
in San Diego for a book reading.

01:38:41.148 --> 01:38:42.916
Perkins elementary is a school

01:38:42.983 --> 01:38:44.952
in San Diego with more than 30%

01:38:45.019 --> 01:38:46.687
of their students that are

01:38:46.754 --> 01:38:48.689
homeless, and the other 70% that

01:38:48.756 --> 01:38:50.924
are low income and once, while

01:38:50.991 --> 01:38:52.860
the principal was walking me out

01:38:52.926 --> 01:38:54.695
after I'd finished the book

01:38:54.762 --> 01:38:55.329
reading, he happened to mention

01:38:55.396 --> 01:38:56.864
to me that the school

01:38:56.930 --> 01:38:58.632
unfortunately had to let go of

01:38:58.699 --> 01:39:00.534
their athletics coach. Now, this

01:39:00.601 --> 01:39:01.168
really got to me because during

01:39:01.235 --> 01:39:02.836
that same time I was really

01:39:02.903 --> 01:39:04.571
getting into basketball and I

01:39:04.638 --> 01:39:05.205
knew how much basketball really

01:39:05.272 --> 01:39:06.874
changed my life. I became more

01:39:06.940 --> 01:39:08.542
confident in myself, more

01:39:08.609 --> 01:39:09.076
physically active and more

01:39:09.143 --> 01:39:10.911
mentally healthy. And knowing

01:39:10.978 --> 01:39:12.746
that these kids at this school

01:39:12.813 --> 01:39:13.380
wouldn't have that same chance

01:39:13.447 --> 01:39:16.583
to fall in love with the sports

01:39:16.650 --> 01:39:17.117
the same way I did, really

01:39:17.184 --> 01:39:18.952
pulled on my heart strings. So I

01:39:19.019 --> 01:39:20.788
felt inclined to do something

01:39:20.854 --> 01:39:22.589
about it. So for the rest of

01:39:22.656 --> 01:39:23.223
that year, I became a volunteer

01:39:23.290 --> 01:39:26.527
coach for Perkins Elementary. I

01:39:26.593 --> 01:39:27.094
coached between 6 to 8 kids

01:39:27.161 --> 01:39:28.829
every Wednesday for on an hour

01:39:28.896 --> 01:39:30.964
and a half. I had no intention

01:39:31.031 --> 01:39:32.900
to make this a nonprofit. I just

01:39:32.966 --> 01:39:34.668
wanted to do good to the

01:39:34.735 --> 01:39:35.302
community. But when I discovered

01:39:35.369 --> 01:39:37.071
the impact, this extra 1.5 hours

01:39:37.137 --> 01:39:38.906
per week had on these kids, I

01:39:38.972 --> 01:39:42.643
decided to make a change. These

01:39:42.710 --> 01:39:44.945
kids were. Besides playing

01:39:45.012 --> 01:39:46.547
sports and becoming more

01:39:46.613 --> 01:39:47.147
physically active, these kids

01:39:47.214 --> 01:39:48.682
became friends with each other

01:39:48.749 --> 01:39:50.684
and even outside of the sports

01:39:50.751 --> 01:39:51.285
clinic, they were hanging out

01:39:51.352 --> 01:39:52.886
and having fun. Plus that they

01:39:52.953 --> 01:39:54.822
genuinely wanted to play sports.

01:39:54.888 --> 01:39:57.057
On the last day they asked me,

01:39:57.124 --> 01:39:58.959
when are you going to come back

01:39:59.026 --> 01:40:00.861
next? Next week? Next year? They

01:40:00.928 --> 01:40:02.830
genuinely wanted this, and that

01:40:02.896 --> 01:40:04.698
prompted me to do some more

01:40:04.765 --> 01:40:05.299
research about the situation.

01:40:05.366 --> 01:40:06.867
And over the summer I discovered

01:40:06.934 --> 01:40:09.036
that approximately 125 schools

01:40:09.103 --> 01:40:10.704
in San Diego have more than 70%

01:40:10.771 --> 01:40:12.773
of their students that are low

01:40:12.840 --> 01:40:14.708
income. And of that, I contacted

01:40:14.775 --> 01:40:16.677
around six and all those schools

01:40:16.744 --> 01:40:18.779
told me that they don't have a

01:40:18.846 --> 01:40:20.647
structured athletics program.

01:40:20.714 --> 01:40:21.248
This research motivated me to

01:40:21.315 --> 01:40:22.816
create sports for kids. We

01:40:22.883 --> 01:40:24.852
started with one sports clinic

01:40:24.918 --> 01:40:27.020
at Perkins Elementary, and we

01:40:27.087 --> 01:40:28.789
coached almost 80 students that

01:40:28.856 --> 01:40:30.557
year. We gave those kids an

01:40:30.624 --> 01:40:32.559
extra 17 hours of physical

01:40:32.626 --> 01:40:33.193
education that the school would

01:40:33.260 --> 01:40:34.762
not have to provide the

01:40:34.828 --> 01:40:36.930
resources for fast forwarding to

01:40:36.997 --> 01:40:40.801
today, sports for kids runs

01:40:40.868 --> 01:40:41.468
various programs across multiple

01:40:41.535 --> 01:40:43.070
schools in San Diego, and we've

01:40:43.137 --> 01:40:43.670
served almost 500 low income

01:40:43.737 --> 01:40:44.905
students throughout our

01:40:44.972 --> 01:40:46.874
operation. Alongside that, we

01:40:46.940 --> 01:40:50.644
are heavily driven by youth

01:40:50.711 --> 01:40:51.278
volunteers. Our team director of

01:40:51.345 --> 01:40:52.980
Social Media communications and

01:40:53.046 --> 01:40:54.782
outreach are all youth led

01:40:54.848 --> 01:40:56.984
positions. Alongside that, we

01:40:57.050 --> 01:40:58.886
also have a professional coach

01:40:58.952 --> 01:40:59.486
going to these schools during

01:40:59.553 --> 01:41:01.088
our sports clinics to ensure

01:41:01.155 --> 01:41:03.123
that these kids get proper good

01:41:03.190 --> 01:41:05.058
sports education. However, we

01:41:05.125 --> 01:41:06.860
also have youth volunteers

01:41:06.927 --> 01:41:08.762
assist in coaching these

01:41:08.829 --> 01:41:09.396
professional coaches to get the

01:41:09.463 --> 01:41:10.931
youth involved in the face of

01:41:10.998 --> 01:41:14.668
change. There are so many

01:41:14.735 --> 01:41:16.937
stories I like to share with you

01:41:17.004 --> 01:41:17.371
today about my time

01:41:17.438 --> 01:41:18.906
volunteering, coaching and

01:41:18.972 --> 01:41:20.741
leading sports for kids and I'd

01:41:20.808 --> 01:41:22.876
like to share one with you

01:41:22.943 --> 01:41:24.778
before we go to the next

01:41:24.845 --> 01:41:25.412
panelist. And it's about this

01:41:25.479 --> 01:41:27.014
kid named Abraham. Abraham was

01:41:27.080 --> 01:41:28.749
one of our program's most shy

01:41:28.816 --> 01:41:29.349
participants. He navigated his

01:41:29.416 --> 01:41:30.818
way through a physical

01:41:30.884 --> 01:41:32.886
disability all his life, and he

01:41:32.953 --> 01:41:34.855
never really felt comfortable

01:41:34.922 --> 01:41:36.690
participating in sports at

01:41:36.757 --> 01:41:38.859
first. He was very reserved in

01:41:38.926 --> 01:41:39.493
our program, understandably so.

01:41:39.560 --> 01:41:42.796
But as the program moved on and

01:41:42.863 --> 01:41:45.065
he got more comfortable, he

01:41:45.132 --> 01:41:46.800
started to show his true colors.

01:41:46.867 --> 01:41:47.367
He played basketball and he

01:41:47.434 --> 01:41:49.036
really liked it. And by the end

01:41:49.102 --> 01:41:51.171
of the sports clinic, he was the

01:41:51.238 --> 01:41:52.906
team captain. And he was

01:41:52.973 --> 01:41:53.540
shooting three pointers, dunking

01:41:53.607 --> 01:41:56.977
even. And he was it was crazy. I

01:41:57.044 --> 01:41:58.879
mean, he was having the time of

01:41:58.946 --> 01:42:00.781
his life and what astonished me

01:42:00.848 --> 01:42:01.415
the most was that the principal

01:42:01.482 --> 01:42:03.116
pulled me aside and said, I've

01:42:03.183 --> 01:42:05.018
never seen Abraham like this

01:42:05.085 --> 01:42:06.687
before. I'd never seen him

01:42:06.753 --> 01:42:07.254
participate in any physical

01:42:07.321 --> 01:42:08.989
activity, and he doesn't really

01:42:09.056 --> 01:42:10.657
talk to anyone outside of

01:42:10.724 --> 01:42:11.291
sports, so this was a complete

01:42:11.358 --> 01:42:15.162
new side of Abraham that he was

01:42:15.229 --> 01:42:16.997
seeing. And that is what my

01:42:17.064 --> 01:42:18.832
program is all about, bringing

01:42:18.899 --> 01:42:19.433
youth together through sports

01:42:19.500 --> 01:42:21.134
and giving them a space to have

01:42:21.201 --> 01:42:23.003
fun. Sometimes having having fun

01:42:23.070 --> 01:42:25.105
is all kids really need. So

01:42:25.172 --> 01:42:26.907
thank you so much for this

01:42:26.974 --> 01:42:29.009
opportunity, and thank you for

01:42:29.076 --> 01:42:30.811
letting me share my story.

01:42:30.878 --> 01:42:32.980
Senator Newman, with the

01:42:33.046 --> 01:42:35.015
committee's indulgence, I would

01:42:35.082 --> 01:42:37.084
like to recognize Arden's

01:42:37.150 --> 01:42:38.785
parents who are here, and give

01:42:38.852 --> 01:42:39.419
them a round of applause. Just

01:42:39.486 --> 01:42:42.823
an extraordinary young man.

01:42:42.890 --> 01:42:52.766
Principal please be seated. Yeah.

01:42:52.833 --> 01:42:54.835
Is that one working? Yes, yes.

01:42:54.902 --> 01:42:55.435
That's on. Oh, cool. There you

01:42:55.502 --> 01:42:58.805
go. Hi, Rene Ramirez, principal,

01:42:58.872 --> 01:43:02.776
Arminta Street Elementary, I'm

01:43:02.843 --> 01:43:03.377
going to give a boots on the

01:43:03.443 --> 01:43:05.145
ground report on the current

01:43:05.212 --> 01:43:08.782
state of PE and physical

01:43:08.849 --> 01:43:09.316
activity in la USD. I'm a

01:43:09.383 --> 01:43:10.918
principal at an elementary

01:43:10.984 --> 01:43:13.053
school, and I've worked at

01:43:13.120 --> 01:43:13.687
another elementary school. Not

01:43:13.754 --> 01:43:15.289
too far from here. Sixth Avenue

01:43:15.355 --> 01:43:16.957
Elementary and pretty much the

01:43:17.024 --> 01:43:20.794
same has the state of physical

01:43:20.861 --> 01:43:21.395
education has stayed the same,

01:43:21.461 --> 01:43:23.096
at least from my perspective,

01:43:23.163 --> 01:43:24.865
across the district, in

01:43:24.932 --> 01:43:26.967
particular, in elementary

01:43:27.034 --> 01:43:28.969
schools. So as was mentioned

01:43:29.036 --> 01:43:32.806
earlier, there is a requirement

01:43:32.873 --> 01:43:33.340
for 100 minutes weekly of

01:43:33.407 --> 01:43:36.777
physical activity that equates

01:43:36.843 --> 01:43:38.946
to about 20 minutes a day, but

01:43:39.012 --> 01:43:41.181
it doesn't always work that way.

01:43:41.248 --> 01:43:43.050
As some of the panelists said

01:43:43.116 --> 01:43:45.018
earlier, sometimes it's broken

01:43:45.085 --> 01:43:46.787
up to two days, maybe three

01:43:46.853 --> 01:43:48.989
days, and at the same time, the

01:43:49.056 --> 01:43:51.091
quality of that 100 minutes.

01:43:51.158 --> 01:43:53.226
Yes, you know, I can go out and

01:43:53.293 --> 01:43:55.162
monitor in the midst of all of

01:43:55.228 --> 01:43:57.097
the other things that I'm doing,

01:43:57.164 --> 01:43:58.966
like the senator had said and

01:43:59.032 --> 01:43:59.600
all these other things that are

01:43:59.666 --> 01:44:01.201
happening at schools, I have to

01:44:01.268 --> 01:44:07.007
go monitor the PE, taking place

01:44:07.074 --> 01:44:09.142
across grades. First through

01:44:09.209 --> 01:44:11.044
fifth at our school, and it's

01:44:11.111 --> 01:44:15.215
taking place, but the quality of

01:44:15.282 --> 01:44:17.217
it is just not there. And that's

01:44:17.284 --> 01:44:19.119
no fault of the teachers, no

01:44:19.186 --> 01:44:21.254
fault of the district. It is

01:44:21.321 --> 01:44:23.323
what it is. The teachers don't

01:44:23.390 --> 01:44:25.192
come in with that training or

01:44:25.258 --> 01:44:27.227
expertise to give a quality,

01:44:27.294 --> 01:44:31.131
comprehensive, PE program. And

01:44:31.198 --> 01:44:33.100
on top of that, we have, you

01:44:33.166 --> 01:44:35.235
know, an aging population of

01:44:35.302 --> 01:44:37.337
teachers. So those teachers that

01:44:37.404 --> 01:44:39.072
are near the end of their

01:44:39.139 --> 01:44:40.941
career, you know, they just go

01:44:41.008 --> 01:44:43.043
out with a kick ball and say,

01:44:43.110 --> 01:44:43.644
here, that's, that's about the

01:44:43.710 --> 01:44:47.014
extent of the PE program as a

01:44:47.080 --> 01:44:48.949
kickball. So we have plenty of

01:44:49.016 --> 01:44:50.984
kickballs, if we're lucky, we do

01:44:51.051 --> 01:44:51.551
have those young, energetic

01:44:51.618 --> 01:44:54.888
teachers that are coming in out

01:44:54.955 --> 01:44:55.555
of college or wherever, and they

01:44:55.622 --> 01:44:57.391
do have that background. They do

01:44:57.457 --> 01:45:00.961
tend to provide, you know, a

01:45:01.028 --> 01:45:02.996
quality, decent PE program. But

01:45:03.063 --> 01:45:05.298
in terms of comprehensive, you

01:45:05.365 --> 01:45:06.933
know, building teamwork,

01:45:07.000 --> 01:45:07.467
collaboration skills, that

01:45:07.534 --> 01:45:08.902
activity that we just did

01:45:08.969 --> 01:45:09.503
earlier with Playworks is just

01:45:09.569 --> 01:45:13.106
not there. So that is the 100

01:45:13.173 --> 01:45:15.175
minute component, not to mention

01:45:15.242 --> 01:45:17.411
we also have teachers that just

01:45:17.477 --> 01:45:21.181
aren't that out of shape

01:45:21.248 --> 01:45:21.782
themselves so they don't have

01:45:21.848 --> 01:45:23.417
any motivation. So neither will

01:45:23.483 --> 01:45:25.318
the students, so we hear a lot

01:45:25.385 --> 01:45:27.154
about equity. The equity

01:45:27.220 --> 01:45:31.024
component is definitely, a

01:45:31.091 --> 01:45:32.993
concern because as you know,

01:45:33.060 --> 01:45:35.228
students that are in my school

01:45:35.295 --> 01:45:37.197
in particular, over 90% free or

01:45:37.264 --> 01:45:39.299
reduced lunch, our lcap money,

01:45:39.366 --> 01:45:41.401
the money that we could be

01:45:41.468 --> 01:45:45.005
spending on PE teachers or

01:45:45.072 --> 01:45:45.605
physical activity programs we

01:45:45.672 --> 01:45:47.207
have to spend on the social

01:45:47.274 --> 01:45:49.076
emotional development of our

01:45:49.142 --> 01:45:51.011
students because we're now not

01:45:51.078 --> 01:45:53.447
just a education institution.

01:45:53.513 --> 01:45:57.017
We're also a social service

01:45:57.084 --> 01:45:57.517
institution. Schools in

01:45:57.584 --> 01:45:59.286
particular in the inner city,

01:45:59.352 --> 01:46:01.388
have become social service

01:46:01.455 --> 01:46:01.988
institutions. And that's just

01:46:02.055 --> 01:46:03.290
the reality. So we have to spend

01:46:03.356 --> 01:46:07.060
our funding, our lcap money on

01:46:07.127 --> 01:46:08.995
counselors, attendance

01:46:09.062 --> 01:46:09.563
counselors, social workers,

01:46:09.629 --> 01:46:13.300
psychologists, interventionists

01:46:13.366 --> 01:46:13.834
to get the kids caught up

01:46:13.900 --> 01:46:17.204
because most of the kids are at

01:46:17.270 --> 01:46:19.172
least 1 or 2 grade levels

01:46:19.239 --> 01:46:19.773
behind. So the free money that

01:46:19.840 --> 01:46:23.110
we do have, we have to spend on

01:46:23.176 --> 01:46:23.677
social services and social

01:46:23.744 --> 01:46:25.245
emotional services and, whereas

01:46:25.312 --> 01:46:29.116
if we had funding for a PE

01:46:29.182 --> 01:46:31.251
teacher or a play program, that

01:46:31.318 --> 01:46:35.322
would actually motivate students

01:46:35.388 --> 01:46:37.090
to come to school as opposed to

01:46:37.157 --> 01:46:39.192
sending a PSA counselor to the

01:46:39.259 --> 01:46:41.094
door to tell them to go to

01:46:41.161 --> 01:46:41.695
school, they would already be

01:46:41.762 --> 01:46:43.063
motivated because there's

01:46:43.130 --> 01:46:45.165
something there at the school

01:46:45.232 --> 01:46:45.766
that they're good at. There's

01:46:45.832 --> 01:46:47.434
something there that they have

01:46:47.501 --> 01:46:49.202
to look forward to every day.

01:46:49.269 --> 01:46:51.438
They may not be good at reading.

01:46:51.505 --> 01:46:53.340
They may not be good at writing.

01:46:53.406 --> 01:46:55.342
As we know, we all come with a

01:46:55.408 --> 01:46:55.976
different set of talents. Those

01:46:56.042 --> 01:46:57.244
kids that have that physical

01:46:57.310 --> 01:46:57.811
talent, that innate physical

01:46:57.878 --> 01:47:01.381
ability to pick up a basketball

01:47:01.448 --> 01:47:03.116
throw, a football hit, a

01:47:03.183 --> 01:47:07.120
baseball that's been proven that

01:47:07.187 --> 01:47:07.721
that we all have something to

01:47:07.788 --> 01:47:11.124
offer. And so I try to do that

01:47:11.191 --> 01:47:13.093
at my school. I try to give all

01:47:13.160 --> 01:47:13.593
of our students as many

01:47:13.660 --> 01:47:15.195
opportunities as I can for

01:47:15.262 --> 01:47:17.430
success, I work closely with our

01:47:17.497 --> 01:47:19.533
after school program to make

01:47:19.599 --> 01:47:21.201
sure that they're, giving a

01:47:21.268 --> 01:47:23.403
quality sports program at our

01:47:23.470 --> 01:47:25.472
school, because that is our

01:47:25.539 --> 01:47:27.140
sports program is the after

01:47:27.207 --> 01:47:29.209
school program, which they

01:47:29.276 --> 01:47:29.810
aren't always quality either.

01:47:29.876 --> 01:47:33.213
But, moving along to my last

01:47:33.280 --> 01:47:35.515
point I want to make is the

01:47:35.582 --> 01:47:37.450
untapped resource that we're

01:47:37.517 --> 01:47:39.119
missing with these students that

01:47:39.186 --> 01:47:39.719
