01:47:39.786 --> 01:47:41.321
have that ability to do things

01:47:41.388 --> 01:47:43.423
out of the classroom. That's

01:47:43.490 --> 01:47:45.525
what I would like to see more

01:47:45.592 --> 01:47:47.260
support in, because we are

01:47:47.327 --> 01:47:49.196
missing, at least at the

01:47:49.262 --> 01:47:51.131
elementary level, a huge

01:47:51.198 --> 01:47:53.300
opportunity, for, tapping,

01:47:53.366 --> 01:47:57.337
resources in our, in our

01:47:57.404 --> 01:47:59.439
students, the leadership skills

01:47:59.506 --> 01:48:01.541
that come along with these types

01:48:01.608 --> 01:48:05.278
of programs can be seen pretty

01:48:05.345 --> 01:48:07.447
clearly at, at an early age. So

01:48:07.514 --> 01:48:09.382
that's why I'm a firm believer

01:48:09.449 --> 01:48:13.186
in developing these as early as

01:48:13.253 --> 01:48:13.854
we can. At the elementary level.

01:48:13.920 --> 01:48:15.388
We're not seeing enough of the

01:48:15.455 --> 01:48:17.424
state funding for schools. The

01:48:17.490 --> 01:48:23.263
PE tip program. It's all the

01:48:23.330 --> 01:48:23.864
district has. If they didn't

01:48:23.930 --> 01:48:27.667
have that program, we would have

01:48:27.734 --> 01:48:29.369
no PE program. Right now. We

01:48:29.436 --> 01:48:31.504
have 17 PE itinerants for over

01:48:31.571 --> 01:48:35.475
400 schools and that by the time

01:48:35.542 --> 01:48:37.377
they get to each school, it's

01:48:37.444 --> 01:48:39.145
about I think about seven years

01:48:39.212 --> 01:48:39.713
by the time that each one of

01:48:39.779 --> 01:48:41.548
those gets to a school. So we

01:48:41.615 --> 01:48:43.183
would have zero funding if we

01:48:43.250 --> 01:48:45.285
didn't have that money and the

01:48:45.352 --> 01:48:47.254
title for money, of course, but

01:48:47.320 --> 01:48:47.854
we just need more support and

01:48:47.921 --> 01:48:49.489
that's what we're asking for

01:48:49.556 --> 01:48:51.524
here today. And thank you. Thank

01:48:51.591 --> 01:48:55.629
you. Mr. Thank you, Principal

01:48:55.695 --> 01:48:57.163
Ramirez, Doctor Thompson,

01:48:57.230 --> 01:48:59.199
welcome. Hi. Thank you so, is

01:48:59.266 --> 01:49:01.468
this on? Not yet. Not yet. Come

01:49:01.534 --> 01:49:03.637
in. I think so now. Yeah. Good.

01:49:03.703 --> 01:49:07.641
Hi everyone. My name is Hannah

01:49:07.707 --> 01:49:09.309
Thompson. I'm an assistant

01:49:09.376 --> 01:49:09.943
research professor in the School

01:49:10.010 --> 01:49:11.378
of Public Health at UC Berkeley.

01:49:11.444 --> 01:49:13.413
And I've been studying physical

01:49:13.480 --> 01:49:13.947
activity and specifically

01:49:14.014 --> 01:49:15.515
physical education in schools

01:49:15.582 --> 01:49:17.584
for the past 15 years or so. And

01:49:17.651 --> 01:49:19.753
my first job out of college was

01:49:19.819 --> 01:49:21.588
actually as a middle school PE

01:49:21.655 --> 01:49:23.323
teacher in Oakland Unified. And

01:49:23.390 --> 01:49:25.392
I will say I'm grateful that

01:49:25.458 --> 01:49:27.260
this locker room smells better

01:49:27.327 --> 01:49:27.894
than the changing area. And that

01:49:27.961 --> 01:49:29.229
middle school, which I still

01:49:29.296 --> 01:49:29.863
think about sometimes, but that

01:49:29.930 --> 01:49:33.366
job is really what is sort of

01:49:33.433 --> 01:49:35.235
motivated and informed. A lot of

01:49:35.302 --> 01:49:37.237
the work that I have done as an

01:49:37.304 --> 01:49:39.439
academic over the past 15 years

01:49:39.506 --> 01:49:40.106
in partnerships with schools and

01:49:40.173 --> 01:49:41.241
school districts. And to your

01:49:41.308 --> 01:49:43.243
question earlier, Senator

01:49:43.310 --> 01:49:43.777
Newman, the CDC recommends

01:49:43.843 --> 01:49:45.478
something called a comprehensive

01:49:45.545 --> 01:49:47.347
school physical activity plan,

01:49:47.414 --> 01:49:49.449
which is sort of an outline for

01:49:49.516 --> 01:49:50.050
how schools can get students

01:49:50.116 --> 01:49:53.253
those recommended 60 minutes of

01:49:53.320 --> 01:49:55.255
moderate to vigorous physical

01:49:55.322 --> 01:49:55.822
activity during the day. The

01:49:55.889 --> 01:49:57.424
Institute of Medicine actually

01:49:57.490 --> 01:49:57.958
has recommended that that

01:49:58.024 --> 01:50:01.294
happens during the school day,

01:50:01.361 --> 01:50:01.962
specifically because of a lot of

01:50:02.028 --> 01:50:03.697
the play equity issues that have

01:50:03.763 --> 01:50:05.699
been born out in this report,

01:50:05.765 --> 01:50:07.367
because most students don't

01:50:07.434 --> 01:50:09.235
actually have opportunities

01:50:09.302 --> 01:50:09.836
outside of school. And of that

01:50:09.903 --> 01:50:11.404
school comprehensive of that

01:50:11.471 --> 01:50:12.038
comprehensive school, physical

01:50:12.105 --> 01:50:13.239
activity plan, physical

01:50:13.306 --> 01:50:15.375
education is really the only

01:50:15.442 --> 01:50:15.875
opportunity that affects

01:50:15.942 --> 01:50:17.644
students throughout their school

01:50:17.711 --> 01:50:21.381
career, right? Elementary school

01:50:21.448 --> 01:50:21.982
students have recess. Not all

01:50:22.048 --> 01:50:23.616
students live in a neighborhood,

01:50:23.683 --> 01:50:25.385
or it's accessible to walk or

01:50:25.452 --> 01:50:27.420
bike to school. Not all students

01:50:27.487 --> 01:50:27.988
participate in after school

01:50:28.054 --> 01:50:31.324
programs. So PE really from a

01:50:31.391 --> 01:50:33.526
public health perspective, is

01:50:33.593 --> 01:50:35.295
really the most equitable

01:50:35.362 --> 01:50:35.862
opportunity we have to reach

01:50:35.929 --> 01:50:37.630
students, regardless of their

01:50:37.697 --> 01:50:41.434
background and to help them get,

01:50:41.501 --> 01:50:42.068
you know, physical activity in

01:50:42.135 --> 01:50:43.803
the present day. But to really

01:50:43.870 --> 01:50:45.538
learn the skills that facilitate

01:50:45.605 --> 01:50:47.741
being an active adult, to going

01:50:47.807 --> 01:50:49.609
on and being active later in

01:50:49.676 --> 01:50:51.478
life. And so when I wanted to

01:50:51.544 --> 01:50:53.546
just mention two studies that

01:50:53.613 --> 01:50:55.482
we've done over the past few

01:50:55.548 --> 01:50:57.350
years in California, the first

01:50:57.417 --> 01:50:59.352
was a survey of how many

01:50:59.419 --> 01:51:01.254
elementary, single subject

01:51:01.321 --> 01:51:03.256
credentialed elementary PE

01:51:03.323 --> 01:51:03.890
teachers we actually have in in

01:51:03.957 --> 01:51:07.260
our public schools here in

01:51:07.327 --> 01:51:07.794
California. This was right

01:51:07.861 --> 01:51:09.662
before Covid, and half of our

01:51:09.729 --> 01:51:11.531
school districts in California.

01:51:11.598 --> 01:51:13.666
So over 300 school districts

01:51:13.733 --> 01:51:15.468
that educate elementary students

01:51:15.535 --> 01:51:16.069
did not have a single subject

01:51:16.136 --> 01:51:17.504
credentialed PE teacher on

01:51:17.570 --> 01:51:21.374
staff. So most PE was being

01:51:21.441 --> 01:51:21.875
taught by Multi-subject

01:51:21.941 --> 01:51:23.610
Elementary School teachers who

01:51:23.676 --> 01:51:25.612
maybe got 1 to 2 years of PE

01:51:25.678 --> 01:51:27.480
training during their

01:51:27.547 --> 01:51:28.114
credentialing program. We also

01:51:28.181 --> 01:51:29.516
found that schools with a higher

01:51:29.582 --> 01:51:31.618
enrollment of minoritized

01:51:31.684 --> 01:51:33.553
students were least likely to

01:51:33.620 --> 01:51:35.388
have PE teachers, and schools

01:51:35.455 --> 01:51:37.624
with more lower income students

01:51:37.690 --> 01:51:39.259
were less likely to have PE

01:51:39.325 --> 01:51:39.859
teachers, so real equity issue

01:51:39.926 --> 01:51:41.661
there. We took it a step further

01:51:41.728 --> 01:51:43.596
and then looked at the

01:51:43.663 --> 01:51:45.465
association between having a PE

01:51:45.532 --> 01:51:45.932
teacher and students

01:51:45.999 --> 01:51:46.566
cardiorespiratory fitness, their

01:51:46.633 --> 01:51:49.369
heart health and schools that

01:51:49.436 --> 01:51:50.036
had PE teachers had students who

01:51:50.103 --> 01:51:51.571
were healthier, who had who

01:51:51.638 --> 01:51:52.138
performed better on tests of

01:51:52.205 --> 01:51:55.375
aerobic capacity. So having PE

01:51:55.442 --> 01:51:57.811
teachers is there's a clear lack

01:51:57.877 --> 01:52:01.448
in California and that is one

01:52:01.514 --> 01:52:03.383
way to open up the pipeline. I

01:52:03.450 --> 01:52:03.983
do a lot of work with the New

01:52:04.050 --> 01:52:05.385
York City Department of

01:52:05.452 --> 01:52:06.019
Education, which is the largest

01:52:06.086 --> 01:52:07.620
school district in the country.

01:52:07.687 --> 01:52:09.489
They they serve as a great model

01:52:09.556 --> 01:52:11.758
for the 5% of their schools used

01:52:11.825 --> 01:52:12.392
to be in compliance with their

01:52:12.459 --> 01:52:13.793
state PE law, and now they have

01:52:13.860 --> 01:52:15.662
a huge number of schools in

01:52:15.728 --> 01:52:17.363
compliance through some of the

01:52:17.430 --> 01:52:18.031
work that they've done. So there

01:52:18.098 --> 01:52:19.766
are models out there that exist

01:52:19.833 --> 01:52:21.601
to doing PE better. We just have

01:52:21.668 --> 01:52:22.168
some opportunities to follow

01:52:22.235 --> 01:52:25.505
those. The second study I wanted

01:52:25.572 --> 01:52:26.106
to mention quickly is I'm sure

01:52:26.172 --> 01:52:27.841
many of you know, because we

01:52:27.907 --> 01:52:29.542
have PE is one of the only

01:52:29.609 --> 01:52:31.411
subjects where we have a minute

01:52:31.478 --> 01:52:31.978
mandate here in California

01:52:32.045 --> 01:52:33.546
several years ago, about 140

01:52:33.613 --> 01:52:35.648
school districts in California

01:52:35.715 --> 01:52:37.750
were sued by a lawyer for being

01:52:37.817 --> 01:52:39.586
non-compliant with our state PE

01:52:39.652 --> 01:52:41.654
law. And this, the lawyer made

01:52:41.721 --> 01:52:43.723
millions of dollars directly

01:52:43.790 --> 01:52:45.391
from schools that schools had to

01:52:45.458 --> 01:52:47.527
pay to him for being

01:52:47.594 --> 01:52:49.696
non-compliant. We actually went

01:52:49.762 --> 01:52:51.464
out and studied the impact of

01:52:51.531 --> 01:52:52.098
this lawsuit. We talked to lots

01:52:52.165 --> 01:52:55.435
of school district

01:52:55.502 --> 01:52:56.035
administrators, lots of school

01:52:56.102 --> 01:52:57.504
district principals to ask them

01:52:57.570 --> 01:52:59.439
how they felt about the lawsuit.

01:52:59.506 --> 01:53:00.039
They didn't like the approach,

01:53:00.106 --> 01:53:01.808
but they liked the fact that all

01:53:01.875 --> 01:53:03.643
of a sudden now people were

01:53:03.710 --> 01:53:05.478
talking about PE and they felt

01:53:05.545 --> 01:53:07.447
like it was able to be elevated

01:53:07.514 --> 01:53:08.114
up their priority list. Oh, this

01:53:08.181 --> 01:53:09.682
actually is something that's

01:53:09.749 --> 01:53:11.484
going to happen that has to

01:53:11.551 --> 01:53:12.051
happen, and we will get in

01:53:12.118 --> 01:53:13.686
trouble if it doesn't happen

01:53:13.753 --> 01:53:15.488
right. So this speaks to that

01:53:15.555 --> 01:53:16.122
accountability piece, right? I'm

01:53:16.189 --> 01:53:17.624
not saying lawsuits are the

01:53:17.690 --> 01:53:18.291
solution. They're certainly take

01:53:18.358 --> 01:53:19.726
money away from schools.

01:53:19.792 --> 01:53:21.394
However, we do need a stronger

01:53:21.461 --> 01:53:21.995
system of accountability and

01:53:22.061 --> 01:53:23.696
some actual, penalties and or

01:53:23.763 --> 01:53:27.400
benefits if you do actually

01:53:27.467 --> 01:53:29.602
comply with the law. The second

01:53:29.669 --> 01:53:31.738
thing we also found, again, sort

01:53:31.804 --> 01:53:33.406
of supporting what we had seen

01:53:33.473 --> 01:53:33.973
in the earlier study is that

01:53:34.040 --> 01:53:35.475
schools that were parties to the

01:53:35.542 --> 01:53:37.744
lawsuit, we saw increases in

01:53:37.810 --> 01:53:38.278
student cardiorespiratory

01:53:38.344 --> 01:53:39.546
fitness in those schools because

01:53:39.612 --> 01:53:41.681
they actually started doing PE.

01:53:41.748 --> 01:53:42.282
So there was a direct benefit

01:53:42.348 --> 01:53:45.552
seen from actually doing PE,

01:53:45.618 --> 01:53:47.654
again, borne out in students

01:53:47.720 --> 01:53:48.154
heart health, which is

01:53:48.221 --> 01:53:48.755
something, you know, we care

01:53:48.821 --> 01:53:49.822
about on so many different

01:53:49.889 --> 01:53:55.428
levels. Thank you and thank you,

01:53:55.495 --> 01:53:55.995
thank you, Doctor Thompson,

01:53:56.062 --> 01:53:57.764
Doctor Parra, welcome. Thank

01:53:57.830 --> 01:53:59.799
you. And I certainly want to

